C.push(say("The data on this is not subtle. Med spas with real membership programs pull twenty to forty percent of their revenue from recurring sources. A hundred members at around two hundred dollars a month is roughly two hundred thirty-eight thousand dollars a year you can count on before anyone books a single extra treatment."));
C.push(say("And members are worth far more than walk-ins. They carry about three times the lifetime value, they come in nearly three times as often, and they spend about thirty-five percent more per visit. Industry data shows each member adds over eleven hundred dollars a year in extra spending, with tox sales up around thirty-one percent and filler up around forty-three percent once they join. The average ticket at a membership spa is about forty percent higher than at a non-member spa."));
C.push(say("Here is why the Beauty Bank matters. When the monthly fee banks instead of vanishing, the client never feels like they are losing money, so they stay. Members are about seventy-eight percent less likely to switch providers. In one case, when a competitor opened nearby, only three percent of members left, compared to thirty-one percent of non-members. The bank is not a giveaway, it is a loyalty lock."));
C.push(say("The four tiers are deliberate. The Glow Up at ninety-nine dollars is a low-friction front door that removes price as an excuse. The Forever Belle at four ninety-nine sets a high anchor that makes the middle tiers feel easy, and it captures your highest spenders. Most people land in the middle, which is exactly where we want them."));
C.push(say("And every discount is calibrated to protect your margin. Injectables run fifty to seventy percent margins, so a member discount there is safe. Skincare and retail are your thinnest margin, so those discounts cap at twenty percent. Tox has a price floor so it never sells below cost. Packages do not stack on membership pricing. Nothing in here sells below what it costs you to deliver."));
C.push(say("The packages do something different. They bring cash in the door up front, they raise the average ticket by thirty to fifty percent, and because the client commits to a series they actually finish their plan, which means better results, better reviews, and more referrals. The Signature Year is the deepest commitment and the deepest savings, and it locks a client in for a full twelve months."));
C.push(say("There is one rule that makes or breaks all of it. Members have to spend their credit on high-margin services, not only on tox. If they only burn credit on product and toxin, net margin can slip under fifteen percent. That is exactly why every tier includes a facial or skin treatment as the signature service. We are steering the value toward the treatments that protect your profit."));

// PART 2
C.push(sectionHeader("Part 2. What the Owner Can Make"));
